1
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:11,767
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:33,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,067
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:41,067
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,133
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:46,333
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:48,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:50,933
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,267 --> 00:00:53,500
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:55,533
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:58,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:00,233
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:03,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:08,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,667
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:12,767
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:15,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:22,233
<i>We will have a party
to remember Sam.</i>

21
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:25,533
<i>I want to honor you all
for a job well done.</i>

22
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:27,300
<i> - For Sam!
</i>- [IN UNISON]  For Sam!

23
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,833
<i>- For Sam!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

24
00:01:30,833 --> 00:01:33,000
<i>Enough! Mission accomplished!
Let's go!</i>

25
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,500
<i>We can't just do nothing
about what happened.</i>

26
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,633
<i> We need to strike back.</i>

27
00:01:35,633 --> 00:01:37,300
<i> We won't let this slide.</i>

28
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:39,900
<i>Thank you so much
for saving our community.</i>

29
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,800
<i> Showing our love for our town</i>

30
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:45,333
<i>can be through
maintaining cleanliness</i>

31
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:47,600
<i> and order in our community.</i>

32
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,867
<i>- Let's start.
- Look at Gabo!</i>

33
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:50,033
<i>You thought I was
Keanu Reeves, didn't you?</i>

34
00:01:50,033 --> 00:01:51,367
<i> I'll go look for a job.</i>

35
00:01:52,033 --> 00:01:53,800
[CHEERING, EXCLAIMING]

36
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,733
<i> Bye!</i>

37
00:01:54,733 --> 00:01:56,600
<i>Miss, these guys
are pickpockets.</i>

38
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:58,100
<i>So, just give us the money
so we won't have any problems!</i>

39
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,400
<i> You're big and strong,</i>

40
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,633
<i>yet you pick
on innocent people.</i>

41
00:02:00,633 --> 00:02:01,933
<i> Thank goodness you're here.</i>

42
00:02:01,933 --> 00:02:03,367
<i> Thank you so, so much.</i>

43
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:07,367
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

44
00:02:07,367 --> 00:02:11,933
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

45
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:14,200
[PAPANG] <i> Did I make
</i> the right decision

46
00:02:14,233 --> 00:02:21,133
<i>to choose Gabo
as an agent of Anino?</i>

47
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:30,167
<i>Pops, how long
do you plan on staying?</i>

48
00:02:30,167 --> 00:02:32,167
<i> It depends...</i>

49
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:36,667
<i>If I find someone who
can join Anino, I'll leave.</i>

50
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:37,567
<i> Pops.</i>

51
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:45,033
[PAPANG] <i> People from various
</i> organizations have tried.

52
00:02:45,033 --> 00:02:49,100
<i>There were soldiers,
police officers, and lawyers.</i>

53
00:02:49,133 --> 00:02:52,333
<i> But they all failed.</i>

54
00:02:52,333 --> 00:02:57,633
<i>So I looked for
an unconventional candidate</i>

55
00:02:57,633 --> 00:02:59,500
<i> whom I could teach</i>

56
00:03:00,767 --> 00:03:05,667
<i> to be worthy of this position.</i>

57
00:03:05,667 --> 00:03:10,367
<i>Sometimes strength and
intelligence are not enough.</i>

58
00:03:10,367 --> 00:03:12,200
- [BOTH GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

59
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,400
[BODY THUDS]

60
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:17,767
[PAPANG] <i> Sometimes,
</i> what a warrior truly needs

61
00:03:17,767 --> 00:03:18,900
<i> is a strong heart.</i>

62
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,933
[INMATES CHEERING]

63
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,433
[BLOWS LAND]

64
00:03:27,433 --> 00:03:28,933
- [CHEERING]
- [METAL BANGING]

65
00:03:30,233 --> 00:03:31,467
[KICK LANDS]

66
00:03:31,467 --> 00:03:33,300
[BLOWS, KICK LAND]

67
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,267
[SHOUTS]

68
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:36,533
[FLESH SQUELCHES]

69
00:03:36,533 --> 00:03:38,233
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

70
00:03:38,233 --> 00:03:39,333
[BLOW LANDS]

71
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:41,267
<i> Hey! He's hurt!</i>

72
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,600
<i> Get Tatang out of here!</i>

73
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,567
<i> Come on!</i>

74
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:48,533
[BLOWS LANDING]

75
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:50,000
[KICKS LAND]

76
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,600
[WARDEN]
<i> I heard you're a tough guy.</i>

77
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,100
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GABO SHOUTS]

78
00:03:56,533 --> 00:03:58,067
[BUBBLES GURGLING]

79
00:03:59,233 --> 00:04:02,333
- [ELECTRIC ZAPPING]
- [GABO GROANING IN PAIN]

80
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:06,033
[SCREAMING]

81
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:07,267
- [THUD]
- [CHAIR THUDS]

82
00:04:07,267 --> 00:04:11,033
- [GRUNTING]
- [KICKS LANDING]

83
00:04:11,033 --> 00:04:12,500
- [BODY THUDS]
- [GRUNTS]

84
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:13,600
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

85
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,767
[KICK LANDS]

86
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:19,367
[PAPANG]  No matter
how strong or tough you are,

87
00:04:19,367 --> 00:04:20,933
<i> you can't take them all on.</i>

88
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:23,567
<i> You need to get out of here.</i>

89
00:04:23,567 --> 00:04:26,567
<i>Gabo, you need to
escape tonight.</i>

90
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:31,267
<i> Gabo, here's the key.</i>

91
00:04:31,267 --> 00:04:33,033
<i> You need to find a way out.</i>

92
00:04:33,033 --> 00:04:36,267
<i>You might not
make it to sunrise.</i>

93
00:04:36,267 --> 00:04:43,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,733
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

95
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,000
[GABO]  I'm not escaping.

96
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,867
<i> I am going to stand by...</i>

97
00:04:54,867 --> 00:04:56,367
<i> the truth.</i>

98
00:04:56,367 --> 00:04:59,767
[PAPANG] <i> You can find
</i> anyone strong and smart,

99
00:04:59,767 --> 00:05:04,267
<i>but not everyone
has a strong will.</i>

100
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:07,400
<i> That's why most people fail.</i>

101
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:15,067
<i>This position does require
brains and strength.</i>

102
00:05:15,067 --> 00:05:17,167
[GABO] <i> I'm sure
</i> you'll be released soon.

103
00:05:17,167 --> 00:05:19,800
<i> We'll all meet again outside.</i>

104
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,133
I think I'm going to die in here

105
00:05:22,133 --> 00:05:24,000
<i>because of how
serious my case is.</i>

106
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,300
<i> Tatang, don't say that.</i>

107
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:27,667
<i> They'll release you one day.</i>

108
00:05:27,667 --> 00:05:29,933
[PAPANG] <i> But most importantly,
</i> it requires someone

109
00:05:29,933 --> 00:05:35,800
<i>with a heart that knows how
to serve the greater good.</i>

110
00:05:35,833 --> 00:05:40,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,667
<i> Good morning, Secretary.</i>

112
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,733
Let's get straight to the point.

113
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:49,400
<i> Have you found someone?</i>

114
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,633
<i> Yes, ma'am.</i>

115
00:05:52,233 --> 00:05:59,167
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

116
00:06:04,433 --> 00:06:07,033
"I strongly recommend that
Anino recruit Gabo..."

117
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:08,300
<i> His name is Gabo.</i>

118
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:14,733
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

119
00:06:14,733 --> 00:06:17,300
<i> Why did you choose a criminal?</i>

120
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,733
<i>Not all criminals
are bad people.</i>

121
00:06:19,733 --> 00:06:22,100
<i> Some of them are also victims.</i>

122
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:28,300
<i>Secretary, this man has
the wit, strength, and courage</i>

123
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:31,333
<i> to be a member of Anino.</i>

124
00:06:31,333 --> 00:06:34,067
<i>We've had a lot of
candidates before.</i>

125
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
<i> Brilliant and skillful ones.</i>

126
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,767
<i>Some with combat
and military qualifications.</i>

127
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:45,867
<i>NLEA agents, lawyers,
Special Forces.</i>

128
00:06:45,867 --> 00:06:47,267
<i> Where are they now?</i>

129
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:51,800
Either they died or betrayed us.

130
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:55,100
[PAPANG] <i> You're right.
</i> They failed us.

131
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,767
<i>So I went for someone
unconventional.</i>

132
00:06:57,767 --> 00:06:59,167
<i> Someone different.</i>

133
00:06:59,167 --> 00:07:02,933
<i> Gabo is unwaveringly loyal.</i>

134
00:07:02,933 --> 00:07:04,600
<i> He would never betray us.</i>

135
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:07,733
<i>His life has
revolved around prison.</i>

136
00:07:07,733 --> 00:07:09,133
<i> I wouldn't be surprised</i>

137
00:07:09,133 --> 00:07:12,533
if he became a traitor one day.

138
00:07:12,533 --> 00:07:15,933
<i>Carlotta, you can't
judge a person</i>

139
00:07:15,967 --> 00:07:18,200
<i> based on their past,</i>

140
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:22,967
<i>without knowing
who they really are.</i>

141
00:07:27,467 --> 00:07:28,833
<i> - I'm still not convinced.
</i>- [FOLDER THUD]

142
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:32,833
<i>He still has a lot
of challenges to overcome</i>

143
00:07:32,833 --> 00:07:35,233
<i>before we can present him
to the president.</i>

144
00:07:35,233 --> 00:07:36,900
<i> I promise you,</i>

145
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:39,333
<i> Gabo will succeed.</i>

146
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:44,567
<i>I'll personally train him
until he's truly ready.</i>

147
00:07:45,633 --> 00:07:52,667
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,433
Pops, it seems Gabo
isn't taking the mission

149
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:56,967
we're about
to give him seriously.

150
00:07:56,967 --> 00:07:58,333
Let's wait for him.

151
00:07:58,333 --> 00:07:59,800
I'm sure he'll show up.

152
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:04,400
I told you that guy from
Ginintuang Lupa is unreliable.

153
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,800
He's all flattery
and empty talk.

154
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,867
He never keeps his word.

155
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,033
Gabo isn't the right person
to entrust

156
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:13,100
with such a huge
responsibility and mission.

157
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,700
He'll only put us
in danger, Pops.

158
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:18,633
I still haven't lost hope.

159
00:08:18,633 --> 00:08:20,767
I've met a lot of people

160
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,733
and tested many of them.

161
00:08:23,433 --> 00:08:28,067
But Gabo has the qualities
of a true warrior

162
00:08:28,067 --> 00:08:32,300
who has the heart to fight
for the oppressed.

163
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:36,000
Pops, let's test Gabo's
other abilities, too.

164
00:08:36,367 --> 00:08:38,833
Once Gabo's mission begins,

165
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:43,000
we'll see if he can handle
being an Anino.

166
00:08:43,067 --> 00:08:46,067
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

167
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:48,133
[GATE CREAKING OPEN]

168
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:05,267
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:09:05,267 --> 00:09:06,733
[DOOR OPENS]

170
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,033
Pops, Gabo is here.

171
00:09:11,367 --> 00:09:18,300
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:09:20,433 --> 00:09:22,467
Why didn't you show up
yesterday?!

173
00:09:22,467 --> 00:09:24,233
Didn't I tell you there was
a message for you?!

174
00:09:24,233 --> 00:09:25,167
What, Gabo?

175
00:09:25,833 --> 00:09:26,967
You didn't read it?

176
00:09:28,267 --> 00:09:29,300
I did.

177
00:09:29,867 --> 00:09:32,100
But a major problem
came up in our area,

178
00:09:32,467 --> 00:09:34,233
and I had to save the people.

179
00:09:34,633 --> 00:09:36,000
That's your problem.

180
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,200
You haven't even started,
and you're already messing up.

181
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:41,067
See! Gabo is good
at handling trouble.

182
00:09:41,067 --> 00:09:42,933
But when you give him
a mission, Pops,

183
00:09:42,933 --> 00:09:44,200
he'll screw it up.

184
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,733
Enough. That's enough.

185
00:09:47,433 --> 00:09:50,600
Gabo, I didn't like
what you did.

186
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:55,433
You should have prioritized
your responsibilities here.

187
00:09:55,433 --> 00:09:57,200
You should have prioritized

188
00:09:57,200 --> 00:10:01,233
your mission duties
here in Anino.

189
00:10:01,667 --> 00:10:04,267
Pops, I hope you can forgive me.

190
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:06,367
I didn't mean for this
to happen.

191
00:10:06,367 --> 00:10:08,500
There was just a huge problem
in our area.

192
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,133
If I hadn't helped the people,

193
00:10:10,133 --> 00:10:11,233
many would have died.

194
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,433
And my family would've been
caught up in it, too.

195
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,633
I understand, Gabo.

196
00:10:16,167 --> 00:10:21,400
That means you prioritized
helping others.

197
00:10:21,467 --> 00:10:28,367
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

198
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:32,433
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:10:34,933 --> 00:10:36,233
[SAM] Just put it back in there.

200
00:10:37,967 --> 00:10:41,067
Pa, I'll just go around
the neighborhood

201
00:10:41,067 --> 00:10:42,800
so we can get more garbage.

202
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:43,867
Okay, Gloria.

203
00:10:43,867 --> 00:10:46,933
We'll take care of things here
while you're gone.

204
00:10:46,933 --> 00:10:49,433
- Okay.
- Ask Tolits to come with you.

205
00:10:49,433 --> 00:10:51,700
- Don't walk around alone.
- Right.

206
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,933
- He's there.
- Tolits!

207
00:10:55,733 --> 00:10:57,167
Can you come with me?

208
00:10:57,167 --> 00:10:58,933
Let's walk around.
There might be garbage left.

209
00:10:58,933 --> 00:11:00,467
Sure! No problem.

210
00:11:00,467 --> 00:11:02,033
Uh, Tekla.

211
00:11:03,467 --> 00:11:06,333
We'll go with Gloria.

212
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:09,633
What you'll do is
you'll stay beside Gloria.

213
00:11:09,667 --> 00:11:12,033
So, there'd be two
beautiful women in front.

214
00:11:12,033 --> 00:11:13,667
- Wow!
- I like that!

215
00:11:13,667 --> 00:11:16,267
[BINOY] Their tandem will be
wife and...

216
00:11:17,167 --> 00:11:19,200
the hopeful!

217
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:20,633
Haha, is it funny?

218
00:11:20,633 --> 00:11:22,067
Wow! We have two muses!

219
00:11:22,067 --> 00:11:24,067
- Wow, muse!
- That's too much!

220
00:11:24,067 --> 00:11:26,133
Yes, yes, enough of that!

221
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,333
Do you want me to hit you
with an uppercut?

222
00:11:28,333 --> 00:11:30,667
- [LAUGHS]
- I have my own plans!

223
00:11:30,667 --> 00:11:32,467
Okay, go on now.

224
00:11:32,467 --> 00:11:33,900
- Go on.
- Take care, dear.

225
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,100
Come back soon
so you can have a snack.

226
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,833
- Mm-hmm.
- Okay!

227
00:11:37,833 --> 00:11:39,067
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

228
00:11:39,067 --> 00:11:40,533
Tekla, let's go!

229
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:42,833
- Baby, let's go!
- We're weak without you!

230
00:11:42,867 --> 00:11:44,967
- You really are--
- Let's go! Time's running!

231
00:11:44,967 --> 00:11:46,067
She's calling you!

232
00:11:46,067 --> 00:11:47,733
[MAMENG] Hey! Leave Tekla alone!

233
00:11:47,733 --> 00:11:49,233
Gabo's wife is so kind!

234
00:11:49,233 --> 00:11:51,133
Oh, don't be too kind!

235
00:11:51,133 --> 00:11:53,233
You'll get to heaven soon!

236
00:11:53,233 --> 00:11:55,200
[TOTO] Oh, sweetie. Can you
make me some coffee?

237
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,667
- I'm sleepy.
- Sure.

238
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:58,633
Twinkle!

239
00:11:58,633 --> 00:12:01,067
Give me more juice!
Put lots of ice.

240
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:04,633
Oh, sweetie!

241
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:08,133
I didn't know
you have a new boss?

242
00:12:09,033 --> 00:12:11,267
Okay. I'll bring it there.

243
00:12:11,267 --> 00:12:12,833
Hurry up!

244
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:16,733
Oh! You're really
something, huh?

245
00:12:16,767 --> 00:12:18,967
So demanding!
Telling me to rush?

246
00:12:18,967 --> 00:12:20,533
You're acting like my boss?

247
00:12:20,533 --> 00:12:22,467
- So much yapping!
- [TWINKLE SCOFFS]

248
00:12:23,167 --> 00:12:24,867
Are you giving me an attitude?

249
00:12:25,633 --> 00:12:27,067
Do we have an issue here?

250
00:12:27,067 --> 00:12:28,367
Yes!

251
00:12:28,367 --> 00:12:30,367
You've hurt Toto's feelings.

252
00:12:30,367 --> 00:12:31,833
You owe him!

253
00:12:31,833 --> 00:12:33,667
With everything you said
about him!

254
00:12:33,667 --> 00:12:39,033
You weren't able to foresee
that we have a problem, madam?

255
00:12:39,033 --> 00:12:41,167
You know, that's the
problem with you.

256
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:45,933
My clients, if I hurt them,
they take it personally.

257
00:12:45,933 --> 00:12:50,167
Why? Am I at fault for what
will happen to your lives?

258
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:53,567
Is it my fault that you're poor?

259
00:12:53,567 --> 00:12:56,533
- [GASPS]
- The juice!

260
00:12:58,867 --> 00:13:01,433
- [PINKY] Isobel!
- Ma'am, Miss Pinky is here.

261
00:13:01,433 --> 00:13:03,633
Hi, my friend.

262
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:05,067
Welcome back.

263
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:08,533
- So, how was your trip?
- Oh, it was really good.

264
00:13:08,533 --> 00:13:10,567
By the way, Isobel,

265
00:13:10,567 --> 00:13:13,233
how was the
memorial service of Sam?

266
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,700
Well,

267
00:13:15,667 --> 00:13:18,833
we managed to pull through even
though it was painful for me.

268
00:13:19,667 --> 00:13:21,367
But I have to accept it.

269
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,900
Isobel.

270
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:25,533
I bought a little something
for you.

271
00:13:25,533 --> 00:13:28,033
- Oh, really?
- I'm sure this will

272
00:13:28,033 --> 00:13:31,767
always remind you of Sam. Look!

273
00:13:32,067 --> 00:13:35,500
Oh! How nice! Letter S!

274
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:36,867
Oh yes!

275
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:42,400
It looks like Sam's necklace
that Madam Rosa took.

276
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:45,533
[INHALES SHARPLY]
I mean, borrowed.

277
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:46,533
Borrowed?

278
00:13:46,533 --> 00:13:47,667
Madam Rosa did?

279
00:13:48,633 --> 00:13:51,167
Well, I don't know. Maybe...

280
00:13:51,167 --> 00:13:54,300
That's her way
of connecting with Sam?

281
00:13:56,067 --> 00:13:58,233
- Can be.
- Oh.

282
00:13:59,733 --> 00:14:01,333
- Pinky?
- Hmm?

283
00:14:01,733 --> 00:14:03,967
Is Madam Rosa for real?

284
00:14:03,967 --> 00:14:06,200
She's for real!
What are you talking about?

285
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:09,067
Her predictions about me
came true!

286
00:14:10,267 --> 00:14:12,367
What are her predictions?

287
00:14:12,367 --> 00:14:13,667
She said,

288
00:14:13,667 --> 00:14:14,967
during this trip,

289
00:14:14,967 --> 00:14:18,967
I will be able
to close a big business deal!

290
00:14:18,967 --> 00:14:23,100
That's why I bought something
for Madam Rosa! Look!

291
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:26,167
I'm sure she'd love this. Look!

292
00:14:26,167 --> 00:14:29,433
- Jade bangles!
- Mm!

293
00:14:30,367 --> 00:14:32,167
What other predictions
does she have for you?

294
00:14:32,633 --> 00:14:35,400
Well, she had
a lot of predictions

295
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:38,133
about business deals
that will come true.

296
00:14:38,133 --> 00:14:41,833
So far, Isobel, everything
she predicted about me,

297
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:44,533
came true.

298
00:14:44,533 --> 00:14:46,933
Starting from January.

299
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:51,500
She said that there was a
project that was stolen from me

300
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,667
that will be given back.

301
00:14:53,667 --> 00:14:57,300
She said that the project
was really meant to me.

302
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:59,167
So, I got it back.

303
00:14:59,167 --> 00:15:01,133
In February,

304
00:15:01,133 --> 00:15:04,900
I asked her about
a robbery in the office.

305
00:15:04,933 --> 00:15:09,700
True enough, I discovered
the thief in my company

306
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:12,400
through an audit.

307
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:15,567
[RICARDO] That's all
I've been waiting for, Manny.

308
00:15:16,967 --> 00:15:18,933
What's your use
if you can't replace

309
00:15:18,933 --> 00:15:20,800
the restraining order
against the demolition?

310
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:24,900
Sir, our man on the inside
has retired.

311
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:26,800
But don't worry,
I'm talking to someone else.

312
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,433
I don't need your explanation.

313
00:15:28,867 --> 00:15:30,800
Max did her share.

314
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:34,033
The people in Ginintuang Lupa
have already signed!

315
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,867
Does she need to fix this too?

316
00:15:36,867 --> 00:15:37,833
No, sir.

317
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,567
Well, then hurry!

318
00:15:39,567 --> 00:15:41,267
We're losing money by the day.

319
00:15:41,767 --> 00:15:43,833
I don't want
my money to sit idle!

320
00:15:44,267 --> 00:15:49,467
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

321
00:15:50,567 --> 00:15:52,200
- [PANTING]
- This is heavy!

322
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:54,300
Here!

323
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:56,400
- This is the pedicab!
- Where?

324
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,033
- Here!
- Huh?

325
00:15:58,033 --> 00:16:00,933
Are you blind? It's broken!

326
00:16:00,933 --> 00:16:03,100
Sir Elton can fix that!
Let's bring it to him!

327
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,533
That's nothing to him!

328
00:16:04,533 --> 00:16:06,033
- Come on. Let's take it!
- Come on.

329
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:08,833
- Come on.
- Go on. Fix that.

330
00:16:08,867 --> 00:16:10,567
- Fix that.
- Here!

331
00:16:10,567 --> 00:16:11,800
- Give it here.
- What's that?

332
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:12,933
Will that still work?

333
00:16:12,933 --> 00:16:14,367
Let's pile them.

334
00:16:14,367 --> 00:16:16,300
- That's heavy!
- Leave it to us, Gloria!

335
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:17,933
Hey. Hurry up!

336
00:16:17,933 --> 00:16:19,300
- Hurry up!
- There!

337
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:20,733
- Get it.
- There!

338
00:16:20,733 --> 00:16:22,967
Instead of us
finishing work early...

339
00:16:22,967 --> 00:16:23,967
Don't worry.

340
00:16:23,967 --> 00:16:26,967
I am used to this kind of work.

341
00:16:26,967 --> 00:16:28,567
I've got this, son!

342
00:16:28,567 --> 00:16:30,500
[ESTONG] That is why
you married mama.

343
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:33,500
This drainage is cleaner
than your mom's heart!

344
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,833
Stop it!

345
00:16:34,833 --> 00:16:37,000
I might slap you in the face!

346
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:40,033
That's why-- what are you doing?

347
00:16:40,033 --> 00:16:41,833
Oh, I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

348
00:16:41,867 --> 00:16:43,667
That's banned!

349
00:16:43,667 --> 00:16:47,067
Our area is getting dirty
because of people like you!

350
00:16:47,067 --> 00:16:48,800
Pa, how does it taste?

351
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,700
- Delicious?
- It's bitter!

352
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:53,033
A bit sour
just like your mother!

353
00:16:53,033 --> 00:16:54,200
Deserve!

354
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:56,500
- You deserve that!
- He's saying you're sour, Ma!

355
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:58,800
He's saying you're kind!
Don't give in!

356
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:01,133
- Commodities!
- Oh!

357
00:17:01,133 --> 00:17:02,800
- Okay.
- It won't flood anymore!

358
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:04,300
- [RUDY] Mameng,
- What?

359
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:07,033
You know, Gloria
is really amusing, right?

360
00:17:07,033 --> 00:17:09,700
Of all people,
she who has amnesia

361
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:12,867
is the one who cares the most
about Ginintuang Lupa.

362
00:17:12,867 --> 00:17:15,133
You know, if it was up to me,

363
00:17:15,167 --> 00:17:19,467
I'd rather not have her
memory come back.

364
00:17:19,467 --> 00:17:21,967
So, there'd be someone
who'll take care of Gabo.

365
00:17:21,967 --> 00:17:23,500
- Yes.
- And of course,

366
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:26,033
there'd be someone who'll
fix Ginintuang Lupa.

367
00:17:26,033 --> 00:17:27,900
- I hope.
- Right?

368
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:30,000
But for now, continue working.

369
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,967
Help them out.
I'll go to the market.

370
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:35,000
I'm sure these people
will be hungry.

371
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,300
Can you see what they're doing?

372
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:40,700
Mameng, you might be forgetting.
We're tired and hungry too.

373
00:17:41,133 --> 00:17:44,233
I'm not forgetting that!
How can I?

374
00:17:44,567 --> 00:17:46,367
- There.
- What are we doing here?

375
00:17:46,367 --> 00:17:48,233
- I remembered something, Dante.
- What?

376
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:49,267
Erwin!

377
00:17:49,967 --> 00:17:52,467
Clean this area!
We'll build something there!

378
00:17:52,467 --> 00:17:54,600
- Here, get this,
- Oh, put it there!

379
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,700
Dante. Make it quick, okay?

380
00:17:57,633 --> 00:17:59,300
Here! Come here.

381
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:01,500
This is what
I've told you about.

382
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,833
Okay, just put it here.
Let's put it here.

383
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:06,333
Thank you. Here, here.

384
00:18:07,267 --> 00:18:09,267
- There, there.
- This long?

385
00:18:09,267 --> 00:18:10,767
That's right. That long.

386
00:18:12,433 --> 00:18:13,900
- Mm!
- [SAM] This too!

387
00:18:14,567 --> 00:18:15,933
Tekla, here.

388
00:18:15,933 --> 00:18:17,633
- Hurry up!
- Give it here.

389
00:18:18,367 --> 00:18:21,933
[SAM] There's a sack there!
There might be something inside.

390
00:18:21,967 --> 00:18:24,667
- [SHRIEKING IN FEAR] My god!
- Whoa!

391
00:18:24,667 --> 00:18:26,033
- Roaches!
- Whoa!

392
00:18:26,033 --> 00:18:28,533
- There's so many of them!
- Hey!

393
00:18:28,533 --> 00:18:30,300
- Get down, get down!
- On his back!

394
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:32,100
- Roaches!
-[SAM] There's more on his back!

395
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:33,733
- They're all over me!
- Stop moving!

396
00:18:33,733 --> 00:18:35,500
- [SHRIEKING IN FEAR]
- Where did they come from?

397
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:37,233
[DABOY] Get them off of me!

398
00:18:37,233 --> 00:18:39,233
[TOLITS] Why'd you have
to shake the sack?

399
00:18:39,233 --> 00:18:40,767
- [SHRIEKING CONTINUES]
- [BINOY] Calm down!

400
00:18:40,767 --> 00:18:42,867
- [BINOY] You're all good now.
- [IPE] We got them.

401
00:18:42,867 --> 00:18:44,267
- I said, you're good now!
- [DABOY SHRIEKING]

402
00:18:44,267 --> 00:18:45,667
- Quit whining!
- It's all gone!

403
00:18:45,667 --> 00:18:47,200
- They're gone now.
- They're gone.

404
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,033
- For real?
- Yeah, they're gone.

405
00:18:49,033 --> 00:18:50,233
- Stop whining.
- It's all good.

406
00:18:50,233 --> 00:18:52,367
[SIGHS] Oh, thank god.
Thanks, guys.

407
00:18:52,367 --> 00:18:53,633
You still have some
on your face!

408
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:55,833
- [SHRIEKING]
- [COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:18:55,867 --> 00:18:56,967
- Look here.
- [SLAP LANDS]

410
00:18:56,967 --> 00:19:01,000
- [TEKLA, BINOY GRUNTS]
- [SLAPS LANDING]

411
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
- Hey.
- [DABOY WHIMPERING]

412
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,500
- What now?
- They're gone!

413
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:06,167
[SHRIEKS] Ack! Roaches!

414
00:19:06,167 --> 00:19:08,333
- They're all gone! Drama queen.
- [IPE] They're gone now.

415
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:10,233
- [IPE] They're just roaches!
- How annoying.

416
00:19:10,233 --> 00:19:12,767
[IPE] Scaredy cat. Get up!

417
00:19:12,767 --> 00:19:14,133
- Here's your shirt.
- [IPE] Let's go!

418
00:19:14,133 --> 00:19:16,200
- Come on!
- There's some on your face!

419
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,300
Huh? What?

420
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:22,500
- [SLAPS LANDING]
- Ow! Get them off!

421
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:23,933
There, over there!

422
00:19:23,933 --> 00:19:25,667
- I'll take care of it!
- Whoa!

423
00:19:25,667 --> 00:19:26,867
- Ow!
- Hey, hey!

424
00:19:26,867 --> 00:19:29,133
- [GRUNTING]
- [BROOM THUDDING]

425
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:31,033
[COMICAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

426
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:35,100
You know, I think we need
to expedite the case

427
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:36,933
- against the Zafras.
- I agree.

428
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:38,700
The longer this drags on,

429
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,733
the better our opponents
could prepare against us.

430
00:19:40,733 --> 00:19:42,200
I just can't stomach

431
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,733
that the Zafras mess with us
like it's nothing.

432
00:19:44,733 --> 00:19:46,633
Just what will the people say?

433
00:19:46,633 --> 00:19:49,400
Just what will
the NLEA say about us?

434
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,133
That this agency is useless?

435
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:54,433
Do you think it'll help
if we coordinate with them?

436
00:19:54,433 --> 00:19:55,833
No, Karen.

437
00:19:56,233 --> 00:19:57,933
We won't do that.

438
00:19:58,767 --> 00:20:00,500
[CLATTERING]

439
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,933
We can settle this just fine
on our own.

440
00:20:03,767 --> 00:20:06,167
[INHALES SHARPLY]
We will give justice

441
00:20:06,167 --> 00:20:08,433
to our comrades
here in the NCIA.

442
00:20:08,433 --> 00:20:09,833
The question is,

443
00:20:10,367 --> 00:20:11,733
where are we gonna start?

444
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:15,067
We'll start with...
what happened recently.

445
00:20:15,467 --> 00:20:17,200
And then we trace it back.

446
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:19,667
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

447
00:20:19,667 --> 00:20:21,833
- Reyes, Borromeo.
- Sir.

448
00:20:22,733 --> 00:20:24,133
You guys work together.

449
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:26,400
Secure the CCTV footage

450
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:28,433
of the incident
at the tribute dinner

451
00:20:28,433 --> 00:20:30,900
as well as our encounter
with the Zafras.

452
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,133
- Yes, sir.
- We'll start from there.

453
00:20:33,133 --> 00:20:34,633
Reyes and I
will take care of it.

454
00:20:34,633 --> 00:20:35,733
- Okay.
- Let's go.

455
00:20:35,767 --> 00:20:42,533
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

456
00:20:42,533 --> 00:20:44,067
- [MAXINE] Good morning.
- [AGENT 1] Good morning, ma'am.

457
00:20:44,833 --> 00:20:46,833
[MAXINE BREATHES HEAVILY]

458
00:20:48,833 --> 00:20:51,233
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

459
00:20:51,233 --> 00:20:52,267
Ma'am.

460
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:54,533
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

461
00:20:54,533 --> 00:20:56,567
Are you sure you're fine?

462
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,633
Come on, I was only gone
for a day.

463
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,067
How's it going?
Any developments?

464
00:21:04,067 --> 00:21:05,867
NLEA raided the safe house.

465
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:07,800
They confiscated
the Zafras' gold.

466
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:09,667
Who's handling the case?

467
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:11,433
Sir Umali and Santos.

468
00:21:12,567 --> 00:21:13,633
[SIGHS]

469
00:21:13,633 --> 00:21:18,267
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

470
00:21:18,267 --> 00:21:20,433
- I told you--
- [MAXINE] Excuse me, sir.

471
00:21:21,767 --> 00:21:24,933
When are we going to call
on the Zafras for questioning

472
00:21:24,933 --> 00:21:26,233
on the lost gold?

473
00:21:26,233 --> 00:21:28,100
We do not have
an evidence strong enough

474
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:29,367
against the Zafras yet.

475
00:21:29,867 --> 00:21:31,800
They work neatly.

476
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:33,767
Even suspects? We still
don't have one yet?

477
00:21:33,967 --> 00:21:35,733
There's no suspect yet.

478
00:21:35,733 --> 00:21:38,367
But the investigation
is currently ongoing

479
00:21:38,367 --> 00:21:39,767
at the neighboring towns.

480
00:21:39,767 --> 00:21:41,133
In Ginintuang Lupa?

481
00:21:43,467 --> 00:21:46,067
Maybe we need to go back
and start the search from there.

482
00:21:46,067 --> 00:21:49,233
If you want, I can talk
to Colonel Domingo

483
00:21:49,233 --> 00:21:51,100
so that I can give you a hand.

484
00:21:51,767 --> 00:21:53,333
[SNICKERS]

485
00:21:53,967 --> 00:21:55,133
No need.

486
00:21:55,433 --> 00:21:56,800
We can handle it on our own.

487
00:21:56,800 --> 00:22:03,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

488
00:22:11,533 --> 00:22:12,900
Sir.

489
00:22:12,967 --> 00:22:15,567
Don't you think Max is growing
suspicious of us?

490
00:22:16,967 --> 00:22:19,333
I could care less if she is.

491
00:22:19,333 --> 00:22:20,767
With how long
I've been in office,

492
00:22:20,767 --> 00:22:23,367
I can dodge no matter what
they throw my way.

493
00:22:23,367 --> 00:22:27,267
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES, ENDS]

494
00:22:27,267 --> 00:22:30,733
I called Agent Brioso
who's looking after Sir Delgado.

495
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:31,967
He seems to be recovering well

496
00:22:31,967 --> 00:22:34,800
and looks like he'll be
discharged tomorrow.

497
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:37,133
- Now that is good news, Karen.
- [SIGHS IN RELIEF]

498
00:22:37,533 --> 00:22:39,700
I hope his recovery continues
to be stable.

499
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:41,233
[SIGHS IN RELIEF] Thank god.

500
00:22:41,233 --> 00:22:44,100
Though we're swarmed
with bad news,

501
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:46,600
at least we got a hold
of one good news.

502
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,400
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

503
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:49,567
[BORROMEO] Sir.

504
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:52,367
Reyes and I have already secured
all the CCTV footages

505
00:22:52,367 --> 00:22:53,400
during the encouter.

506
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:56,267
Good. Have it scanned
and run it on the database

507
00:22:56,267 --> 00:22:59,467
so we could see the faces
of the men who attacked us.

508
00:22:59,467 --> 00:23:01,267
Sir, we already did.

509
00:23:01,267 --> 00:23:04,033
However, we almost got nothing
out of the footage.

510
00:23:04,033 --> 00:23:05,500
[SIGHS] That's not an excuse!

511
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:08,367
Rummage through all the profiles
that we've got

512
00:23:08,367 --> 00:23:10,600
who are connected to the Zafras
since day one.

513
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,633
Whether it's the people
who attacked us

514
00:23:12,633 --> 00:23:14,400
or those who went after Sam.

515
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:16,100
As long as they're connected
to the Zafras,

516
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:19,467
-search and capture all of them.
- [THUDS]

517
00:23:19,533 --> 00:23:20,667
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

518
00:23:20,667 --> 00:23:27,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

519
00:23:29,733 --> 00:23:30,800
Gabo.

520
00:23:31,633 --> 00:23:32,800
Take a seat.

521
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:39,800
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

522
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:48,600
You have to understand.

523
00:23:49,100 --> 00:23:51,433
Once you've become
a part of Anino,

524
00:23:51,433 --> 00:23:55,900
you must abide by all its rules.

525
00:23:55,933 --> 00:23:59,000
Your family should not be
your priority.

526
00:24:02,367 --> 00:24:03,467
Pops.

527
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:05,267
He's already got a wife.

528
00:24:06,033 --> 00:24:07,833
It'll be even more troublesome.

529
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:10,933
[LAWIN] Gabo's priority
is different now, Pops.

530
00:24:10,933 --> 00:24:14,833
He'll chicken out when it comes
to his family and wife.

531
00:24:14,833 --> 00:24:18,367
In this job, danger
is inevitable.

532
00:24:18,367 --> 00:24:21,967
Your loved ones
could get involved.

533
00:24:21,967 --> 00:24:24,200
You have to be prepared
for everything.

534
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:26,167
[TOMAS] That's not all, Gabo.

535
00:24:26,167 --> 00:24:28,400
Your entire family
will be sacrificed.

536
00:24:28,833 --> 00:24:30,067
Your life.

537
00:24:30,067 --> 00:24:33,100
Even your closest friends.

538
00:24:34,133 --> 00:24:36,533
And most of all, your wife.

539
00:24:36,533 --> 00:24:39,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

540
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,667
Are you ready for it?

541
00:24:40,667 --> 00:24:44,700
You will be generously awarded
for every mission.

542
00:24:44,933 --> 00:24:49,733
But in exchange, you will have
to sacrifice everything.

543
00:24:49,733 --> 00:24:55,133
So, I need you answer
before you begin, Gabo.

544
00:24:55,133 --> 00:25:02,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

545
00:25:05,467 --> 00:25:07,067
I accept the mission.

546
00:25:07,067 --> 00:25:09,767
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

547
00:25:09,767 --> 00:25:11,267
To become a part of Anino.

548
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:15,833
Because I can't just stand by
watching all these crimes

549
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:21,233
and corruption that is rampant
in our government.

550
00:25:23,267 --> 00:25:25,133
Someone needs to do something.

551
00:25:25,133 --> 00:25:27,367
Someone has to start
that change.

552
00:25:29,267 --> 00:25:30,600
And that will be me.

553
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:33,900
Well then, I'll explain to you

554
00:25:33,900 --> 00:25:37,433
how you'll get started
on your mission.

555
00:25:37,467 --> 00:25:44,433
[STIRRING MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

556
00:25:53,033 --> 00:25:54,433
These are the people
connected to the Zafras

557
00:25:54,433 --> 00:25:56,667
and their illegal businesses.

558
00:25:56,667 --> 00:26:00,033
There are also CCTV grabs
from past encounters,

559
00:26:00,033 --> 00:26:02,333
and not all of them
have confirmed identities.

560
00:26:02,333 --> 00:26:03,667
Oh, not all of them?

561
00:26:03,667 --> 00:26:05,200
But how many have records?

562
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:08,667
Sir, as of now,
20 have confirmed identities.

563
00:26:08,967 --> 00:26:10,167
Can we locate them?

564
00:26:10,167 --> 00:26:11,500
- Affirmative, sir.
- There you go.

565
00:26:11,500 --> 00:26:14,067
We'll round them all up.

566
00:26:14,067 --> 00:26:15,500
But, sir, the problem is

567
00:26:15,500 --> 00:26:16,733
that we don't have solid cases
against them yet,

568
00:26:16,733 --> 00:26:18,133
so we can't arrest them.

569
00:26:18,933 --> 00:26:20,833
I don't care!

570
00:26:20,833 --> 00:26:22,867
The Zafras are already
targeting us,

571
00:26:22,867 --> 00:26:24,767
and we're doing nothing
about it.

572
00:26:24,767 --> 00:26:27,033
That's an embarrassment
to our agency.

573
00:26:27,033 --> 00:26:29,933
So start tracking them down
and arresting them.

574
00:26:29,933 --> 00:26:31,767
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

575
00:26:31,767 --> 00:26:35,867
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

576
00:26:35,867 --> 00:26:39,000
Gabo, watch this carefully.

577
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:43,333
Last year,

578
00:26:43,333 --> 00:26:49,533
35,717 focused crimes
were recorded nationwide.

579
00:26:49,533 --> 00:26:51,633
6,000 were theft cases,

580
00:26:51,633 --> 00:26:53,700
and 3,000 were robberies.

581
00:26:53,700 --> 00:26:56,833
Not all crimes
lead to complaints.

582
00:26:56,833 --> 00:26:59,467
And not all victims
come forward.

583
00:26:59,467 --> 00:27:00,933
People go missing,

584
00:27:00,933 --> 00:27:03,600
but their disappearances aren't
reported to the police.

585
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:05,900
What's worse,
we don't have a complete

586
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:08,100
national list
of missing persons,

587
00:27:08,100 --> 00:27:10,933
especially those whose
disappearances go unreported.

588
00:27:10,933 --> 00:27:12,500
When someone goes missing,

589
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:15,267
it doesn't just mean
one person is affected.

590
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:16,800
One person,

591
00:27:16,800 --> 00:27:18,233
one family,

592
00:27:18,233 --> 00:27:20,933
one case that needs answers.

593
00:27:20,933 --> 00:27:22,900
As time passes,

594
00:27:22,900 --> 00:27:25,567
it becomes harder and harder
to find them.

595
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:29,267
That's just part of what
you have to face, Gabo.

596
00:27:29,267 --> 00:27:36,133
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

597
00:27:36,300 --> 00:27:37,367
<i> If Sam were still alive,</i>

598
00:27:37,567 --> 00:27:41,700
<i>she wouldn't have wanted you
to destroy Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

599
00:27:41,700 --> 00:27:43,367
<i> But she's dead, Isobel!</i>

600
00:27:43,367 --> 00:27:45,333
<i> The people of Ginintuang Lupa</i>

601
00:27:45,333 --> 00:27:48,133
<i>didn't even help her
on the night she died!</i>

602
00:27:48,133 --> 00:27:50,033
<i> Business isn't the only reason</i>

603
00:27:50,067 --> 00:27:52,533
<i>I want Ginintuang Lupa
demolished.</i>

604
00:27:52,533 --> 00:27:54,467
<i> This is our main armory.</i>

605
00:27:54,467 --> 00:27:57,333
<i> Encrypted military-grade pens.</i>

606
00:27:57,333 --> 00:28:00,167
<i>Just one device,
but it's a command center.</i>

607
00:28:00,167 --> 00:28:01,600
<i> A tactical watch</i>

608
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:04,633
<i>integrated with
the car's AI system.</i>

609
00:28:04,633 --> 00:28:07,400
<i>Heavy-duty,
shatterproof lenses.</i>

610
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:11,800
<i>Alex stands for Adaptive
Logistics and Execution.</i>

611
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:15,967
<i>He'll be your primary system
while you're on the road.</i>

612
00:28:15,967 --> 00:28:19,500
<i> Just tell Alex what you need.</i>

613
00:28:19,500 --> 00:28:22,100
<i> You and the car are one.</i>

614
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:25,633
<i>Misty is associated
with a modeling agency.</i>

615
00:28:25,667 --> 00:28:27,200
<i>She's the one you need
to keep an eye on.</i>

616
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:28,833
<i> I promise you,</i>

617
00:28:28,833 --> 00:28:32,400
I'll track them down and rescue
<i> the women they've kidnapped.</i>
